<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmroom</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmroom new &lt;keyword&gt;                        (230)
gmroom new &lt;keyword&gt; in &lt;room@zone&gt;
gmroom new &lt;keyword&gt; in here
gmroom title &lt;gm3|here&gt; &lt;text&gt;
gmroom descr &lt;gm3|here&gt; &lt;text&gt;
gmroom outside &lt;gm3|here&gt; &lt;text&gt;
gmroom list
gmroom free &lt;gm3|here&gt;
</pre>
<p>A game master's rooms, made while the game runs, for an event: a tent 
in a square, a hidden cellar, a backstage where you keep what the event 
brings in. They are named gm1, gm2 and so on, in the zone _gm 
(gm3@_gm), and they are gone at the next reboot. At most 100 can exist 
at once.
</p><p><b>new</b> makes a room called "Inside the &lt;keyword&gt;". With <b>in</b> it 
stands inside that room (or the one you stand in), like a tent: players 
see it there ("A &lt;keyword&gt; is here.") and enter and leave it. Without 
it the room stands on its own; go there and give it exits with set room 
dir-to (see <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Set</a>). Exits go one way, so set one back from the 
other room too, and only in a direction that room doesn't use yet: 
dir-to replaces an exit.
</p><p><b>title</b>, <b>descr</b> and <b>outside</b> set its title, what you see 
inside it, and how it shows in the room around it, one line each.
</p><p><b>list</b> shows the rooms, where each stands and how many players are 
in it.
</p><p><b>free</b> ends a room. Everyone and everything inside, players' 
corpses too, goes to the room it stands in, or else where its first 
exit leads, or else the crypt in Udgaard. Exits that led to it are 
removed. A room with another gm room inside must wait until that one 
is freed.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>gmroom new tent in here
gmroom outside gm1 A patched red tent stands by the well.
gmroom descr gm1 Rugs cover the floor; it smells of incense.
gmroom free gm1
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
